<v Benjamin>OK. I'm going to let him go.
<v Benjamin>好的。我要让他去休息了。

00:51:24.690 --> 00:51:25.590
<v Scott Pinkmountain>Thank you so much.
<v Scott Pinkmountain>非常感谢。

00:51:25.590 --> 00:51:34.640
<v Benjamin>Thank you very much.
<v Benjamin>非常感谢。

00:51:34.640 --> 00:51:49.870
<v Scott Pinkmountain>When I got home, Benjamin finally gave me the names of a few artists who've collaborate with Anthony. I was able to reach three of them. They'd all gotten letters similar to Schandra's saying, I have an autistic son who's fallen in love with your art. Two of them got chocolates.
<v Scott Pinkmountain>我回家后，本杰明最终给了我几个与安东尼合作过的艺术家的名字。我联系上了其中三个人。他们都收到了类似于桑德拉的那种信，说：我有一个爱上你艺术的自闭症儿子。其中两个人收到了巧克力。

00:51:49.870 --> 00:52:07.430
<v Scott Pinkmountain>The only artist I spoke to who actually met Benjamin and Anthony was Tillman Kaiser. They showed up at his gallery show in London last summer. He was also the only one who was able to address our biggest question, the thing we couldn't figure out at Benjamin's. Was Anthony truly engaged with the art his dad was exposing him to?
<v Scott Pinkmountain>我交谈过的唯一一个真正见过本杰明和安东尼的艺术家是蒂尔曼·凯泽。去年夏天他们出现在他在伦敦的画廊展览上。他也是唯一一个能够解决我们最大问题的人（那个我们在本杰明家无法查明的事情）。安东尼真的投入了他父亲向他展示的艺术吗？

