<v Tillman Kaiser>He was standing in front of the canvasses and sculptures and had a look. And I really had the impression that he enjoyed meeting me. And he seemed to be quite interested in the paintings and looked at them one by one.
<v Tillman Kaiser>他站在画布和雕塑前看了一看。我真的觉得他喜欢见到我。他看起来对画作很感兴趣，一幅接一幅地看。

00:52:26.380 --> 00:52:30.270
<v Scott Pinkmountain>Tillman said Anthony even made up his own titles for a couple paintings.
<v Scott Pinkmountain>蒂尔曼说安东尼甚至为几幅画自己取了名字。

00:52:30.270 --> 00:52:52.700
<v Tillman Kaiser>"Elephant Ears." And the other one, he called it "Drug Addiction." I mean, I think it's totally weired what they're doing. But I don't want to judge them, you know? I don't want to say they do bad things.
<v Tillman Kaiser>“大象耳朵”。另一幅，他称之为“药物成瘾”。我是说，我觉得他们做的事情太奇怪了。但我不想评判他们，你知道吗？我不想说他们做坏事。

00:52:52.700 --> 00:53:04.560
<v Scott Pinkmountain>Finally, I met again with Schandra and told her what I'd learned, that Anthony does exist, that he probably has some disorder, that Benjamin seems to be collecting from quite a few artists. She was torn.
<v Scott Pinkmountain>最后，我再次见到桑德拉，告诉她我学到的东西：安东尼确实存在，他可能有一些障碍，本杰明似乎在从相当多的艺术家那里收藏。她感到很纠结。

00:53:04.560 --> 00:53:36.510
<v Schandra Singh>It's like on the one hand, it's really wonderful. I wish maybe it would have been-- I guess, wish that maybe it would have been proposed to me that we have this autistic child, he really responds to art, we're amassing a collection of art for him to learn from, to be inspired from, to realize his own talents. It would be so special if we could do a trade with you, because we know he loves your work. Like, all these things maybe would have helped me kind of understand, as opposed to writing an email saying, you're the one that moves Anthony.
<v Schandra Singh>一方面，这真的很棒。我希望也许它会被——我猜，希望也许它会被提议给我：我们有一个自闭症孩子，他真的对艺术有反应，我们正在为他积累艺术收藏，让他从中学习，从中汲取灵感，让他实现自己的天赋。如果我们能和你做一个交换，那会很特别，因为我们知道他热爱你的作品。所有的这些事情也许会帮我理解，而不是写一封电子邮件说：你是打动安东尼的那个人。

00:53:36.510 --> 00:53:39.260
<v Scott Pinkmountain>And what if that's totally authentic?
<v Scott Pinkmountain>如果那完全是真实的呢？

00:53:39.260 --> 00:54:00.370
<v Schandra Singh>Well, I mean, I think it's a wonderful story then, that he's wanting to do all of this for his children. But it's just like, why did Baker and I feel so awkward when we found out that we both got asked the same thing? Why did we both think it was so much about us, you know?
<v Schandra Singh>嗯，我是说，那是一个精彩的故事，他想为他的孩子们做所有这些。但这只是——为什么贝克和我在发现我们俩都被要求做同样的事情时都感到那么尴尬？为什么我们俩都觉得那很多是关于我们，你知道吗？

00:54:00.370 --> 00:54:13.500
<v Scott Pinkmountain>So yes, Schandra thinks Benjamin could be more transparent with the artists he's contacting. But I agree, if he's doing this for his kids, that's a wonderful story. It's optimistic. And so many artists are optimists.
<v Scott Pinkmountain>所以，是的，桑德拉认为本杰明可以在他联系艺术家时更透明一点。但我同意，如果他是为了孩子做这件事，那是一个精彩的故事。它是乐观的。而且很多艺术家都是乐观主义者。

00:54:13.500 --> 00:54:27.210
<v Scott Pinkmountain>Proof? Schandra's friend Baker, hearing what we discovered in London, still wants to send Anthony a drawing. Two of the other artists I'd spoke to, artists who'd sent Anthony their work, were totally OK with what Benjamin's doing.
<v Scott Pinkmountain>证据？桑德拉的朋友贝克听到我们在伦敦的发现，仍然想给安东尼寄一幅素描。我交谈过的其他两位艺术家（寄给安东尼作品的艺术家）完全同意本杰明所做的事情。

00:54:27.210 --> 00:54:39.730
<v Scott Pinkmountain>And if there's one thing I've learned from this experience it's that, man, artists are an easy mark, because it's so obvious what they want. They want to reach people. Otherwise, why show your art? Why be an artist?
<v Scott Pinkmountain>如果我从这次经历中学到了一点，那就是：天哪，艺术家是容易上钩的人，因为他们想要什么太明显了。他们想接触人们。否则，为什么要展示你的艺术？为什么要成为一名艺术家？

00:54:39.730 --> 00:54:49.250
<v Scott Pinkmountain>So all you have to say is, I'm moved by what you do, or my kid is moved by what you do. So many artists are like, you want to pay me? Great.
<v Scott Pinkmountain>所以你要说的就是：我被你的所作所为打动了，或者我的孩子被你的所作所为打动了。很多艺术家会这样：你想付钱给我？太棒了。

00:54:49.250 --> 00:55:01.740
<v Scott Pinkmountain>But you say you love my work? Even better. Let me send you some.
<v Scott Pinkmountain>但你说你喜欢我的作品？更好。让我寄一些给你。

00:55:01.740 --> 00:55:09.870
<v Ira Glass>Scott Pinkmountain is a composer and musician and writer in Pioneer Town, California. By the way, you can see some of Anthony's artwork at our website.
<v Ira Glass>斯科特·平克山是加利福尼亚先锋镇的作曲家、音乐家和作家。顺便说一下，你可以在我们的网站上看到安东尼的一些艺术品。

